  "narrative": {
    "intro": "Fairwinds Technologies is a federal contractor with $490M in contract obligations in FY2026 to date. Fairwinds Technologies recorded 181 awards this fiscal year and an average award size of $2.7M. Fairwinds Technologies obligations are down 4.1% year over year. Fiscal-year history shows growth leading into FY25 and FY26: FY21 obligations were $1.2M, FY22 obligations were $147M, FY23 obligations were $176M, FY24 obligations were $164M, and FY25 obligations were $511M. Fairwinds Technologies receives the vast majority of FY2026 obligations from the Department of Defense, which obligated $488M. Fairwinds Technologies also received obligations from the Department of Homeland Security in FY2026 to date of $2.2M and from the Department of the Interior of $30.9K. Fairwinds Technologies sells primarily into a small set of NAICS markets: Bare Printed Circuit Board Manufacturing with $269M, Other Electronic Component Manufacturing with $135M, and Other Computer Related Services with $78.1M. Fairwinds Technologies shows smaller FY2026 activity in related markets such as Radio and Television Broadcasting and Wireless Communications Equipment Manufacturing with $8.4M.",
    "sections": [
      {
        "heading": "Who are Fairwinds Technologies top buyers?",
        "body": "The Department of Defense is the top buyer, obligating $488M to Fairwinds Technologies in FY2026 to date. The Department of Homeland Security obligated $2.2M and the Department of the Interior obligated $30.9K. The Department of Transportation shows $0 in obligations for FY2026 to date."
      },
      {
        "heading": "What markets does Fairwinds Technologies serve?",
        "body": "Bare Printed Circuit Board Manufacturing is the largest market with $269M in FY2026 obligations to Fairwinds Technologies. Other Electronic Component Manufacturing and Other Computer Related Services are significant markets with $135M and $78.1M respectively. Fairwinds Technologies also has smaller obligations in Radio and Television Broadcasting and Wireless Communications Equipment Manufacturing at $8.4M and in Research and Development in the Physical, Engineering, and Life Sciences at $500."
      }
    ]
